    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9009" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνί̆ερ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unholy, unhallowed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				220
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				769
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				757
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνίερος ἀθύτων πελάνων</span>
			<i>unhallowed because of</i> the unoffered sacrifices, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				146
			</span></i> (all lyr. passages); of a child <i>born out of wedlock,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				461b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>receiving no victims,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					992
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
